18.09.2026
How did we go from ancient mechanical automata to robots that can see, move, learn, drive, explore Mars, and even assist in surgery?

In this video, we slowly explore the complete story of robotics — from early automata, Unimate, and Shakey to computer vision, self-driving cars, humanoid robots, and modern AI-powered machines. We also look at how robots learn through reinforcement learning, simulation, imitation learning, and newer vision-language systems.

Resources:

SRI International — Shakey the Robot
https://www.sri.com/hoi/shakey-the-ro...

NASA — How Perseverance Drives on Mars
https://science.nasa.gov/resource/how...

OpenAI — Solving Rubik’s Cube with a Robot Hand
https://openai.com/index/solving-rubi...

Google DeepMind — RT-2: Vision, Language and Robotic Action
https://deepmind.google/blog/rt-2-new...
