a combination of camera feeds and manual joysticks. The remarkable thing about operating a robotic arm in space is that
1:12:51
1 Stunde, 12 Minuten, 51 Sekunden
the normal physics of gravity don't apply. But the physics of inertia absolutely do. A massive payload doesn't
1:12:59
1 Stunde, 12 Minuten, 59 Sekunden
weigh anything in orbit. But it still has mass. And if you swing it too fast, the momentum can start to rotate the
1:13:07
1 Stunde, 13 Minuten, 7 Sekunden
entire space station. The control algorithms had to account for this in ways that terrestrial robot arms never
