inserted through small incisions. The robot doesn't operate autonomously. The surgeon is in complete control at all
1:14:02
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 2 Sekunden
times. But the robot provides something the human body cannot. Scaled down
1:14:08
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 8 Sekunden
motion, tremor filtering, and endoscopic access through incisions barely a centimeter across.
1:14:16
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 16 Sekunden
Here's what that means in practice. When a surgeon makes a large hand movement at the console, the robot might translate
1:14:25
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 25 Sekunden
that into a tiny precise movement at the instrument tip, maybe a 5:1 or 10:1
1:14:32
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 32 Sekunden
scaling. Human hands have a natural tremor, a few tenths of a millimeter that you barely notice in daily life,
1:14:41
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 41 Sekunden
but that matters enormously when you're operating near a nerve or a blood vessel. The Da Vinci system filters out
1:14:49
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 49 Sekunden
that tremor, producing movements that are supernaturally smooth. And because the instruments are inserted through
1:14:56
1 Stunde, 14 Minuten, 56 Sekunden
tiny ports rather than large incisions, patients experience less pain, less
1:15:03
