3.770 Aufrufe  16.09.2026
Your brain doesn’t simply record reality — it actively builds it.

In this video, we explore how perception really works, from predictive processing and optical illusions to our sense of time, body ownership, memory, dreams, and even the feeling of being a self. Along the way, we look at experiments like the rubber hand illusion and discover why what feels like direct reality may actually be your brain’s best ongoing guess about the world.

Perfect for relaxing, learning, or drifting off to sleep.

Resources:

Nature Reviews Neuroscience — The Free-Energy Principle: A Unified Brain Theory?
https://www.nature.com/articles/nrn2787

Nature — Rubber Hands ‘Feel’ Touch That Eyes See
https://www.nature.com/articles/35784...

PubMed — Elizabeth Loftus: Planting Misinformation in the Human Mind
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/16027...

National Library of Medicine — Memory, Sleep and Dreaming: Experiencing Consolidation
https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles...
