16.814 Aufrufe  09.08.2026
The entire history of the evolution of life explained slowly and calmly for sleep.
Travel backward through nearly four billion years of evolution, from modern humans and our closest primate relatives to the earliest mammals, reptiles, fish, multicellular organisms, single-celled life, and the ancient common ancestors shared by every living thing on Earth.
In this long and relaxing science documentary, we explore the history of evolution, natural selection, common ancestry, DNA, mutations, mass extinctions, the Cambrian explosion, the evolution of animals, human evolution, and the origins of life.
Instead of treating evolution as a simple ladder leading toward humans, we follow the enormous branching tree of life, moving backward through time and meeting the common ancestors that connect us with other species.
How far back do you have to travel before humans and chimpanzees become one family?
What ancestor connects us to other mammals?
Why do the bones in your arms still carry the basic anatomical pattern inherited from ancient fish?
How did simple cells eventually give rise to animals, forests, dinosaurs, mammals, primates, and humans?
And if we continue traveling backward far enough, where does the history of life finally lead?
Along the way, we explore some of the most important transitions in the evolution of life on Earth: early hominins, the rise of mammals, the transition from water to land, the development of complex multicellular organisms, the Cambrian explosion, early eukaryotic cells, photosynthesis, the Great Oxidation Event, LUCA, and the earliest stages of biological evolution.
We also look at the evidence scientists use to reconstruct this enormous history, including fossils, comparative anatomy, genetics, DNA, molecular clocks, geology, and evolutionary biology.
From the first primitive life to the extraordinary diversity of organisms alive today, this is a slow journey through almost four billion years of life, evolution, extinction, adaptation, and common ancestry.
Relax, get comfortable, and follow the story of the evolution of life on Earth with Quantara Explains.

The information used to create this video was researched and cross-checked using multiple authoritative scientific and historical sources, including established works in evolutionary biology, paleontology, genetics, and the history of life.
Selected sources and further reading:
• Richard Dawkins - The Ancestor's Tale: A Pilgrimage to the Dawn of Evolution 
• Charles Darwin - On the Origin of Species 
• Neil Shubin - Your Inner Fish 
• Douglas J. Futuyma & Mark Kirkpatrick - Evolution 
• Ernst Mayr - What Evolution Is 
• Nick Lane - The Vital Question 
• Andrew H. Knoll - Life on a Young Planet 
• Smithsonian Institution - Human Origins research and educational resources 
• University of California Museum of Paleontology - Understanding Evolution 
• Peer-reviewed research in evolutionary biology, genetics, paleontology, and Earth history 
Information was compared across multiple sources where appropriate. The narrative structure, explanations, organization, and original presentation were created specifically for Quantara Explains.
