13.244 Aufrufe  19.09.2026
Take a slow, relaxing journey through the hidden shortcuts your mind uses every day. This video explores cognitive biases like anchoring, confirmation bias, hindsight bias, the availability heuristic, sunk costs, overconfidence, the Dunning-Kruger effect, and the bias blind spot—and explains why these mental shortcuts exist in the first place.

Along the way, we look at famous psychology experiments, key researchers, and how these biases quietly shape our memories, decisions, relationships, money, risk, and everyday thinking.

Resources:

Tversky & Kahneman — Judgment Under Uncertainty: Heuristics and Biases
https://www.science.org/doi/10.1126/s...

Nobel Prize — Daniel Kahneman
https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/eco...

APA Dictionary of Psychology — Confirmation Bias
https://dictionary.apa.org/confirmati...

APA Dictionary of Psychology — Bias Blind Spot
https://dictionary.apa.org/bias-blind...
