It's a really great video. Thanks a lot. But I am not sure if an understimulated/bored immunsystem plays such a big role for  developing autoimmune diseases. It is described that virus infections (for example Eppstein Bar) or bacterial infections of the urine tract can trigger autoimmune diseases as well as stress and that the microbiome in  the gastrointestinal tract plays an essential role. The hypothesis of a bored immunsystem might be true for allergies but the role for autoimmune diseases is probably low. Genetic factors play a role in both, allergies and autoimmune diseases. Since stress and nutritional factors and overweight (fat - inflammation) have changed the last years they might play a role for increasing cases of allergies and autoimmune diseases. I am really looking forward to listen to more videos. They are really good!!! The way it explains things is amazing.

