14:58
symbiosis. Over millions of years, they became inseparable. That small trapped
15:05
bacterium evolved into what we now know as the mitochondrian.
15:10
This is not just a story. The evidence is inside you right now. If you look
15:15
closely at a mitochondrian, you will find it has its own DNA separate from
15:20
the nucleus. And that DNA is circular just like a bacteriums. It has its own
15:27
