Avatarbild
Every Confusing Psychological Paradox Explained Slowly (For Sleep)
KI


Cosmo Explains Psychology und Cosmo Explains

Abonniert

173





16.841 Aufrufe  10.09.2026
Why does the mind sometimes work against itself? This relaxing deep dive explores some of psychology’s most confusing paradoxes — from the paradox of choice and thought suppression to happiness, cognitive dissonance, overconfidence, self-awareness, and the Dunning-Kruger effect.

Discover why more choices can make decisions harder, why trying not to think about something can make it return, why chasing happiness can leave us less happy, and why feeling confident doesn’t always mean being correct — all explained slowly for a calm, sleep-friendly experience.

Resources:

Iyengar & Lepper — When Choice Is Demotivating
https://doi.org/10.1037/0022-3514.79....

Wegner et al. — Paradoxical Effects of Thought Suppression
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/3612492/

Mauss et al. — Can Seeking Happiness Make People Unhappy?
https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles...

Kruger & Dunning — Unskilled and Unaware of It
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10626...
