I related to the Woman to Worship him but was able to grow away from that by writing a story where I originated as the receiver of the attention and instead became a distant but fulfilled best friend of the situation. I think journalling and writing are often recommended as good for the psyche and I hope everyone continues to grow in their own creativity. It is nice haven't been able to explore and seek for the woman to worship me, but it feels great knowing that I can become a Uke and Nage for my next Uke and Nage(Aikido training partners and philosophy). The deflation of my fantasy(the woman that would worship me) has been a long year process and I feel discomfort when knowing that I am not actively seeking the woman that would worship me and play into all of my active mother roles. My mother adored me and showered me with excellent care and attention. When I was 21 I met a powerful and caring father figure that lead the household very rationally and respected all situations with a strong sense of humanity, he was hardened but had many different life circumstances and that allowed me to really move away from the daydreaming about a woman to worship my fantasies. My mental illness had always had a hyper-sexual element that enhanced my desire to seek for a woman to worship me. I recommend exploring all parts of the psyche and not going into any state of denial. It took an effort to write this position and not be in denial about my commonality, I definitely want you to grow, but not denying anything, and I know I will also continue my search for a woman to worship me but I also know I can recognize this and grow towards a relationship based on more communication and negotiation, rather than demanding my attention be returned through manipulative management. That's why I recommend Aikido you and your. In aikido your girlfriend performs the technique on you and you perform the technique on her, it feels very intimate and that role reversal seems to grow the psyche a good amount.

