“Do not play the expected gender role,  but rather create the one that suits you.”
Law 13 - Aimlessness
20:56
Law 13 - The Law of Aimlessness  - Advance with a sense of purpose
21:02
He who has a why to live can  bear with almost any how.  —Friedrich Nietzsche
21:09
As opposed to animals, who can use their  instincts to steer clear of danger, humans   must rely on their own judgments. As long as we  follow our instincts moment by moment, we will  
21:18
wander aimlessly, which will lead us to dead ends.  Developing a sense of purpose, discovering our  
21:24
calling in life, and using that knowledge to guide  us in our decisions will prevent such a fate.  
21:30
We gain a deeper understanding of  ourselves, our tastes and preferences.
21:36
When we lack purpose, we  become increasingly insecure.   When we have a sense of purpose, we are  less likely to suffer from depression.
21:44
It is best to avoid hiring or working with  people who are motivated by a false purpose,   as their unproductive energy  will tend to drag you down.  
21:52
If you surround yourself with people who have  a strong purpose, they will pull you upward.
21:58
“Operating with a high sense of  purpose is a force multiplier...The   many sides to your character are channeled into  this purpose, giving you more sustained energy.”
22:09
Strategies for Developing a High Sense of Purpose  In developing a sense of purpose,  you will encounter many challenges.  
22:16
Others may distract you from finding your true  direction by instilling doubt in your heart.
22:21
You can overcome these obstacles By  using the following five strategies | Discover your calling in life. Often, the earliest signs of your true calling  can be located in the earliest years of your life.
22:31
Consider moments in your life when you  felt natural and at ease doing certain   tasks or activities, as if you were  running with the wind at your back.
22:38
When you pursue your purpose,  some people will criticize you,   some may be helpful, but  others may just come from envy.  
22:46
Take their negative opinions and judgements of  you as motivation and fuel for your purpose.
22:52
Associating with people who  have a strong sense of purpose   will allow you to absorb their purposeful energy.
22:59
Create a ladder of descending goals.  If you set long-term goals, you will  gain incredible clarity and resolve. 
23:05
However, if you look at all the steps necessary  to reach them from your current position,   they are likely to generate anxiety.  If you want to manage such anxiety,  
23:14
you should have a ladder of smaller goals  extending down from the present to the future. Finally, dedicate uninterrupted  time with your work.  
23:22
Find states of flow. Focus on the work  and not the recognition or reward.
23:29
The Lure of False Purposes We are all aware of how insignificant we are   in a universe with billions of others. In order to  feel connected to something bigger than ourselves,  
23:39
we need to feel larger than ourselves. As human  nature is, however, many people are searching  
23:45
for meaning and a sense of transcendence  on the cheapest and easiest terms possible.
23:51
Throughout history, without a true purpose,  humans have been attracted to five common   types of false purposes. The pursuit of pleasure: 
23:59
We often think of work as just a boring necessity  of life. Ultimately, we are motivated by avoiding  
24:05
pain and finding as much pleasure as possible  outside of work. Our pursuit of pleasure takes  
24:11
many different forms, such as sexual activities,  recreational stimulants, and entertainment.
24:18
By operating with a sense of purpose,  we understand the importance of placing   limits on ourselves rather than  overstimulation of the senses.
24:27
Causes and cults As human beings we have a deep desire to believe  in something, and with a lack of unifying beliefs,  
24:34
cults fill that void. Groups whose disciples  are vague in their objectives should be viewed  
24:40
with caution, as the group is more than  likely just about releasing emotions.
24:46
Money and success A person's pursuit of money and status  often motivates and focuses them.  
24:51
Despite this, many of the richest  anMoney and success will naturally  
24:58
flow to you if you focus on your goals  and maintain a high sense of purpose.
25:04
Attention: As a way to feel more important,   people have always desired fame and  attention. This false sense of purpose,  
25:12
however, has been greatly democratized  with the help of social media.  By cultivating a strong sense of purpose and  creating projects which are naturally appealing,  
25:22
we will have a much better  chance of attracting attention. Cynicism
25:27
"Man would rather have the void as purpose  than be void of purpose."-Friedrich Nietzsche
25:34
Cynicism, the conviction that  existence is meaningless,   has the effect of leading to "the void  as purpose." Politics, pandemics, and  
25:42
old beliefs all contribute to this type of fake  purpose, which is growing in popularity nowadays.
Law 14 - Conformity
25:54
Law 14 : The Law of Conformity -  Resist the Downward Pull of the Group
26:00
“When people are free to do as they  please, they usually imitate each other.”  —Eric Hoffer
26:07
The social personality is the different  person that we become when we are operating   in groups of people, it is a side to our  character that we are rarely even aware of.
26:17
In a group, we unconsciously  imitate what others say and do. There is no positive or negative  side to the social force;  
26:24
it is simply an aspect of our human nature.   The Individual Effect The desire to fit in: 
26:33
In order to feel like we belong  or fit in with the group,   we tend to alter our appearance or  adopt its ideas, beliefs and values.
26:41
The need to perform: We become actors in the group,   guiding what we say and do so that other team  members accept us as loyal members of the team.
26:50
Emotional contagion:  We experience the contagiousness  of emotions through the group.  
26:56
The group map compel you to act in ways that  you would otherwise not, if you were alone. Hypercertainty: 
27:02
In the group, we are driven to make urgent  decisions and support them. This gives us a   sense of certainty that makes us more open  to taking risks. You should never give up  
27:12
your ability to doubt, reflect, or consider  other options that differ from the group.
27:18
“The larger the group and the more  established the culture over time,   the more likely it will control  you than the other way around.”
27:25
Group Dynamics  You must study the following dynamics  in the groups to which you belong: 
27:31
Group culture: Groups carry some dynamic of culture,   from countries with long standing traditions,  all the way down to a company or even an office. 
27:42
An ideal state will always be the center  of the group's culture and spirit.
27:47
Group rules and codes: The distressing effects of disorder and   anarchy are experienced by all groups. Therefore,  standard rules and how to conduct oneself quickly  
27:57
emerge and are established. They are not written  down, but are implied by all group members.
28:04
The group court: In any chimpanzee colony, you   will observe an alpha male and other chimpanzees  adapting their behavior with him, following,  
28:13
imitating, and trying to strengthen their bonds  with him. Essentially, this is a prehuman version  
28:19
of the court, or the social dynamic. Despite the difference in appearance,   the behavior and strategies of the  courtiers continue to be very similar.
28:29
The group enemy: In the groups you belong to,   you will almost certainly find some sort of enemy  or villain to fight, be it human or otherwise.
28:39
Group factions: As a group becomes large enough,   individuals start to form factions. A faction, left unchecked, can grow so  
28:47
powerful it takes control of the leaders.  By creating an enthusiastic and unifying   environment in the group, factions become less  desirable, which tightens the whole group.
28:58
The Court and the Courtiers In any group dynamic there will be a struggle for  power. There will be some form of group court,  
29:08
with an alpha leader at the top and subordinate  leaders with whom people try to get close to.
29:13
Understanding the court's dynamics is crucial. Be able to identity the types of  courtiers, such as the Intriguer 
29:20
(who appears loyal to the group,  but is secretly accumulating power),  
29:25
the Stirrer (who hides their  envy to cause conflict),   the Gatekeeper (who use their position to control  the flow of information and isolate the leader).
29:37
The Reality Group Here are 5 strategies if   you want to create a healthy group dynamic Instill a collective sense of purpose. 
29:46
You must capture and channel that social force  that compels people to belong and to fit in.   This Can’t be a vague purpose it must  be clearly stated and publicized. 
29:55
Assemble the right team of lieutenants. Your fear of delegating authority will   be your biggest obstacle. Developing a team  of lieutenants with the skills that you lack  
30:03
must be the very first thing you do. Let information and ideas flow freely. 
30:08
Communication is the lifeblood  of any group. Encourage open   discussion to build the members' trust. Infect the group with productive emotions. 
30:17
You should radiate a sense of  determination that permeates the group.   In the face of setbacks, you are the one that  keeps pressing forward and solving problems. 
30:25
Forge a battle-tested group. When faced with a crisis, you want   to find out how tough a person is from the inside.  Test the people in your team with some relatively  
30:34
challenging tasks and shorter deadlines than  usual and see how they respond under pressure.
