23.872 Aufrufe  15.09.2026
Ever wondered how programming languages actually turn human-readable code into instructions a computer can understand?

This video slowly explores the evolution of programming languages, from machine code, assembly, and early compilers to FORTRAN, LISP, C, Java, Python, JavaScript, Rust, and beyond. We also look at compilers, interpreters, memory management, type systems, concurrency, WebAssembly, and how AI-assisted coding is changing programming today.

Resources:

IBM — History of Fortran
https://www.ibm.com/history/fortran

LLVM — Building a Programming Language & Compiler
https://llvm.org/docs/tutorial/MyFirs...

The Rust Programming Language — Understanding Ownership
https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-0...

MDN — WebAssembly Concepts
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/d...
