A digital CPU have a reduced or complex instruction set with a specific operation code and with some operations we can access memory with address numbers and each single address have 8 bits. To use larger values in memory we have to combine the bits of two or four addresses.

One of the most important things of digital CPUs are the flag register with special bits inside, instructions that set or clear one or more bits of the flag register and instruction that use the bits of the flag register like conditional jump instruction that jump to an other memory address inside the executable mashine code, if one or more bits of the flag register are set or not set, or it is not jumping and continue with the next  instruction to perform the execution flow.



