@TheZafootz
vor 3 Monaten
Good information video and good history lesson as well, but lacks intellectual insight on electricity and fails to point out where we might have got things not entirely right. 

For example its said in this video that atoms have a balance of electric charge and when "electrons" are shaved off giving the object a net positive charge because it has less electrons then it needs to remain neutral. And when this unbalance of charge causes electrons to jump from a negatively charged source to the positive charge source, stating electric charge only moves from negative charge to positive charge. And there is no flow of positive charge towards negative charge. But is this entirely true? No it is not because when we look at a step leader come from the clouds and get close to the ground with very fast fps cameras we have been able to capture snips of positive streamers coming up from out of the ground reaching up for the step leader. And when a step leader and positive stream connect, then there is a massive discharge of electric current from the clouds to the ground. Now if electricity was what they call "electrons" that only move from negative to positive charge then how come we see positive streamers come up from out of the ground when a step leader gets close to the ground? This evidence tells us that there is some sort of positive charge that reaches for negative charge the same as negative charge reaching for positive charge. Now going off the story of negative electrons always moving from negative to positive, how is it possible that positive streamers are able to come up from out of the ground when negative electrons are supposed to be the only free-flowing part of the atom that moves electric charge? How does positive charge move in positive streams when those parts of the atom are supposed to be locked in the nuclei of the atom?

Another thing they fail to understand and explain incorrectly is the Photo-electric effect that they claim is evidence that light is a particle. When you take a glass rod and rub it with silk and negatively charge the rod, then rub that rod on a piece of metal that has some very thin metal sheets on it called "leaf's" these leaf's tend to stick out and stay that way as long as the negative charge stays in the metal leaf sheets. But when you shine x-ray light on the negatively charge leaf's, they collapse and no longer stick out and to keep their atomic structure of the atom they explain that light is a particle that slams into the metal leaf's and bounce electrons off the leaf's and discharge them causing them to collapse. They say this to protect their atomic structure that they seem to worship and never want to change, so they change the facts around to fit their atomic structure when the real facts is this. The x-ray light does not send little particles of light "photons" and knock off electrons from the metal leaf's causing them to discharge, that is NOT what is happening. What happens is the x-ray light causes the molecules in the air around the metal leaf's to become charged some positively some negatively. When this happens the negative charge in the leaf's find a path to discharge into the positively charged ions in the air around the leaf's and that is what causes the discharge.

Sadly we live in a world that does not like to let go of old ideas even when their is evidence that tells us otherwise, so they twist facts to fit the narrative instead of taking on the challenge of figuring out where they went wrong with their model. This is why things like "light" and "electricity" are hard to understand, because they paint the wrong picture on how things actually work and paint it with a custom picture that fits their established ideas already instead of embracing new ones that are more accurate then their ideas. Old habits die-hard, well so do scientific established ideas around invisible phenomena's like old ideas on electricity that are not entirely correct die-hard as well.
