1:51:11
ideas that began with a Hungarian prodigy wondering whether there was a
1:51:17
mathematics of poker bluffing. And lying here thinking about all of this as you settle deeper into your
1:51:24
pillow and the details begin to soften at the edges. There's something quietly profound about the whole enterprise.
1:51:31
Because game theory at bottom isn't really about games. It's about interdependence.
1:51:38
It's about the simple inescapable fact that almost nothing you do in life happens in a vacuum. Your choices ripple
1:51:46
outward. They affect other people and their choices affect you and the fabric
1:51:53
of social life. All the cooperation and competition and trust and betrayal and
1:51:59
