Slowly drift through the most confusing ideas about gravity, from Newton’s law and free fall to orbits, black holes, spacetime, tides, and gravity waves. A calm, sleep-friendly explanation designed to make gravity feel simple, peaceful, and easy to understand.
Cosmo Explains traces the historical evolution of our understanding of gravity, from Aristotelian concepts to Galileo's experiments with motion and inertia. The exploration continues into Newton's universal gravitation and Einstein's groundbreaking insights, examining how these brilliant minds fundamentally reshaped our knowledge of space, time, and the underlying forces governing the cosmos.
