Each of those machines is a direct descendant of Widow's row of tubes and of those sloshing radio frequency
2:39:34
2 Stunden, 39 Minuten, 34 Sekunden
cavities we met when we first learned to use the same push twice.
2:39:39
2 Stunden, 39 Minuten, 39 Sekunden
And then there's the scan I promised to come back to. It's called a PET scan, which stands for positron emission
2:39:47
2 Stunden, 39 Minuten, 47 Sekunden
tomography. Here's how it works, and it brings together almost everything in our story. It starts with a cyclron,
2:39:56
2 Stunden, 39 Minuten, 56 Sekunden
Lawrence's spiral machine, often sitting right in the hospital. The cyclron fires
2:40:02
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 2 Sekunden
protons at a target and turns some of the atoms there into a radioactive form of florine.
2:40:11
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 11 Sekunden
That radioactive flororine is attached to a kind of sugar and the patient receives a small amount of it. Once
2:40:19
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 19 Sekunden
inside the body, the sugar travels to wherever the body is burning energy fastest, which often includes places
2:40:28
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 28 Sekunden
affected by cancer or heart disease. And the radioactive florine does something remarkable.
2:40:36
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 36 Sekunden
It gives off posetrons, antimatter, tiny amounts of it created inside the
2:40:44
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 44 Sekunden
patient's body. Each positron travels only a very short distance before it
2:40:51
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 51 Sekunden
meets an ordinary electron. And just as we learned, they annihilate.
2:40:57
2 Stunden, 40 Minuten, 57 Sekunden
The two particles vanish and their mass becomes energy in the form of two
2:41:03
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 3 Sekunden
particles of light flying off in exactly opposite directions. The PET scanner is
2:41:10
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 10 Sekunden
a ring of detectors around the patient catching those pairs of light particles.
2:41:16
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 16 Sekunden
Every time two detectors on opposite sides catch a pair at the same instant, the scanner knows the annihilation
2:41:24
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 24 Sekunden
happened somewhere on the line between them. Collect millions of those lines and you can build up a detailed picture of where the sugar went inside the body.
2:41:35
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 35 Sekunden
Doctors can see disease that would otherwise be hidden. So, here's a machine descended from Lawrence's
2:41:42
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 42 Sekunden
palmsized cyclron creating antimatter inside a human being on purpose to save lives.
2:41:51
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 51 Sekunden
I think it's fair to say that JJ Thompson did not see that coming. When you add it all up, there are tens of
2:41:59
2 Stunden, 41 Minuten, 59 Sekunden
thousands of particle accelerators in the world. When Sheihi gave her talk, the count was more than 35,000.
2:42:08
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 8 Sekunden
Something like 45% of them are used for radiotherapy.
2:42:13
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 13 Sekunden
Most of the rest are in industry, treating and scanning things, hardening the rubber in tires, changing the colors
2:42:21
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 21 Sekunden
of gemstones, cleaning dirty drinking water, making the tiny structures in computer chips.
2:42:29
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 29 Sekunden
only a small fraction are giant research machines like the LHC.
2:42:36
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 36 Sekunden
Shehi says that when she wants to know which problems matter most, she doesn't have to look very far. She just reads
2:42:43
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 43 Sekunden
the morning news. climate change, food and water shortages, diseases we still can't cure, aging
2:42:52
2 Stunden, 42 Minuten, 52 Sekunden
populations, security threats, even she jokes, the chance of an asteroid hitting the
2:43:00
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten
planet. And she says she chose to spend her life on particle accelerators of all things because she believes what we've
2:43:08
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten, 8 Sekunden
learned from these machines can help with some of those very problems. and accelerator physicists are still pushing into new territory.
2:43:18
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten, 18 Sekunden
Shehi describes two frontiers. There's the energy frontier, which is where the LHC lives. Higher and higher energies to
2:43:27
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten, 27 Sekunden
create heavier and rarer particles, and there's the intensity frontier, which is where she works. On the
2:43:35
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten, 35 Sekunden
intensity frontier, the goal is to deliver more particles, many more. One of the main reasons to want very intense beams is to make neutrons.
2:43:46
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten, 46 Sekunden
Neutrons are the uncharged particles found inside atomic nuclei, and they're wonderful for looking inside materials
2:43:55
2 Stunden, 43 Minuten, 55 Sekunden
because they pass through many things easily and interact with atoms in revealing ways.
2:44:02
2 Stunden, 44 Minuten, 2 Sekunden
If you slam a very intense beam of protons into a heavy metal target, neutrons come spraying out.
2:44:11
2 Stunden, 44 Minuten, 11 Sekunden
In England, there's a neutron source called ISIS which has been running for more than 30 years.
2:44:19
2 Stunden, 44 Minuten, 19 Sekunden
