 Aufrufe  
29.09.2026
What does it really mean to be an empath? In this video, we explore the science behind empathy, highly sensitive people, emotional contagion, and why some people seem to feel other people's emotions more intensely.

We look at sensory processing sensitivity, how the brain responds to other people's pain, the difference between empathy and compassion, and why emotional regulation and healthy boundaries may matter more than simply trying to block out other people's feelings.

Resources:

Tania Singer et al. — Empathy for Pain
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14976...

Bianca Acevedo et al. — The Highly Sensitive Brain
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25161...

Tania Singer & Olga Klimecki — Empathy and Compassion
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/25247...

Greven et al. — Sensory Processing Sensitivity Review
https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/30639...
